load @/code/space/hyperbolic/plane
  find hyperbolic-plane

# The axioms of hyperbolic geometry. Hyperbolic geometry keeps every axiom of Euclid except the parallel postulate, the
# shared core called absolute (or neutral) geometry: the incidence axioms (two points determine a line), the order
# axioms (betweenness on a line), the congruence axioms (segments and angles can be copied), and the continuity axioms
# (Dedekind completeness, the Archimedean property). To these it adds the HYPERBOLIC PARALLEL AXIOM in place of
# Euclid's: through a point not on a given line there pass at least two distinct lines that never meet the given line.
# From this one change everything follows: triangles have angle sum below two right angles, the deficit equal to the
# area; similar triangles are congruent (no rescaling); the plane has constant negative curvature; and there are
# infinitely many regular tilings instead of three. The form carries the hyperbolic plane the axioms govern.
form hyperbolic-axioms
  link plane, like hyperbolic-plane
